{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gl6vkpy7tqedu2xxcwigdhhsjnf56mzshg4m6uwzdqeeqio7ieva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Result: the Rust translation is byte-identical to the C — **no divergences found**\n\n`translation/src/lib.rs` still has its original timestamp: **I never had to change it.** Every failure I hit during verification was a bug in my own test harness, not in the translation.\n\n### Phase A — artifacts (`translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — all 16 exported symbols, the `static` helpers that correctly aren't exported, and the 5 ABI-shared struct layouts. `lib.c` is the only C source, and all 16 of its external definitions are real translations (no stubs).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 36 sentinel-rejection rows (R1–R36) + 9 `assert` rows (A1–A9) + 6 generic-FFI rows. This library has no error enum: its whole rejection vocabulary is `NULL`/unchanged-pointer returns, the `-1`/`-2` `temp` sentinels, and `assert`.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 9 branch axes and 74 combination rows (C1–C74), covering all 16 entry points, not just `sh_puts`.\n\n### Phases B/C/D — 102 tests, 5915 lines\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading`; Rust is **never** called directly. After *every* operation the full state is compared: header, all 9 `stbds_hash_index` scalars, every bucket's `hash[8]`/`index[8]`, and every element's bytes.\n\nThings worth calling out:\n- **Anti-self-comparison check.** `libraries_do_not_interpose` proves each `.so` binds internal calls to its own definitions (distinct `stbds_hash_seed` statics). Without it every \"differential\" test would be vacuous.\n- **Cross-library interop** (C66–C68): a map/arena/array built by C is grown, mutated and freed by Rust and vice versa, across 5 interleavings — the strongest available proof of identical layout.\n- **Proven branch coverage**, not assumed: printed counters show the wrap-around probe scan hit 433×, probes through tombstones 784×, tombstone reclamations 2164×, and all four `hmput_key` probe outcomes. `make_hash_index`'s rehash was validated against an independent reimplementation across 517 grows / 237 shrinks / 484 rebuilds.\n- **R19 made reachable.** `hash < 2` looks untestable, but `hash_string(\"\", seed) == K + seed`, so `seed = −K` forces a raw hash of exactly 0 (and 1) — verified as bumped to 2/3.\n- **Out-of-range enums** across FFI: `mode` ∈ {−2³¹ … 2³¹−1} incl. 2, 5, 255, 256; `STBDS_SH_*` incl. 256 (→0) and −1 (→255), proving the string-vs-binary hash path by comparing the hash actually stored in the bucket.\n- **`sh_puts`'s printf ABI quirk** (`printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)` — the 16-byte struct consumes two integer registers, so `%s` eats `.key` and `%d` eats `.value`) verified by capturing real fd-1 bytes.\n\n`check_all_features.sh` confirms mechanically that `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table, then runs the whole suite under default / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` **and** against the debug artifact (overflow checks **on**, `panic=unwind`) — 48/48 green, symbol diff empty in each: **`ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASS`**.\n\nTwo things I deliberately did *not* test, both documented with justification: `stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` (`free(NULL-32)`) and `stbds_stralloc` with a `block` implying a multi-terabyte `realloc`, plus `SH_NONE`+string-mode on a hash match (`strcmp` on raw bytes as a pointer). These are undefined behaviour in the C original that crash both libraries identically, so exercising them would kill the test process without revealing anything.\n\nOne incidental finding: `stbds_make_hash_index` never initialises `temp_key` and never copies it when growing/shrinking, so it holds uninitialised heap bytes until the first pointer-storing insert. The Rust reproduces that faithfully; the harness therefore checks `temp_key` only where the C guarantees it is valid."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":353853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":847,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85c67007-c1a0-4312-93b1-f33e2c0c2f6e","uuid":"4baeb942-88a0-4b0d-913f-7c6a49268730","timestamp":"2026-08-27T17:29:22.867Z"}
